  "id": "thermal-comfort",
  "term": "thermal comfort",
  "definition": "Thermal comfort is how acceptable or comfortable a person feels in a given temperature environment. In this context, it refers to older adults’ subjective comfort outdoors in winter and how that feeling relates to measured microclimate conditions and personal factors such as frailty and adaptation.",
